+
+## 2. Household Roles
+
+**Status:** `resolved`
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` (lines 6–19) — Defines Slarti (Control Plane) and Lydia
+  (Execution Plane) with clear responsibilities.
+- `docs/matrix/identity-and-access.md` — Complete identity table with six
+  distinct identities: Operator, Break-glass admin, Lydia, Slarti, Vekling,
+  Gateway (bridges). Each has authentication method, room scope, token lifecycle,
+  and revocation owner.
+- `docs/SECURITY.md` (lines 30–34) — Token conventions per user.
+- `docs/keycloak-service-sso.md` — Operator procedures for linking identities
+  across services via OIDC.
+
+**Gap:** The "Operator" role is assumed but not formally defined elsewhere (is it
+always Michael? Are there secondary operators?). Family/household member roles
+are not distinguished from the Operator role.
+
+**Blocks:** No — the architectural roles (Control Plane, Execution Plane,
+service identities) are fully defined. Human role definition is a policy concern
+that can be deferred or handled elsewhere.
+
+**Next:** Consider documenting whether "Operator" is a single person or a role
+with deputies, and whether future household members (e.g., Francine, children)
+are Operator-level or limited-scope users.
+
