+## 6. Data Ownership and Lifecycle
+
+**Status:** `partially resolved`
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `docs/STORAGE.md` — Overview of three-node storage, capacity plan, backup
+  strategy, NFS export details. Backup strategy has gaps marked "Unknown."
+- `docs/PI_SERVICES.md` (lines 188–258) — Detailed backup scripts for Paperless,
+  PaperlessFrancine, Gitea, Keycloak. Rotation strategies (2-version for
+  Paperless, 7-day for Gitea).
+- `docs/matrix/storage-and-retention.md` — Comprehensive volume inventory,
+  retention policy per category, growth alarms and thresholds, owner matrix,
+  restore inputs.
+- `docs/QNAP_TS559_PRO_II.md` — Storage configuration with 89% capacity usage
+  identified as HIGH risk.
+
+**Gap:** No data lifecycle policy for the overall system:
+- What data is critical vs. disposable?
+- What is the archival policy for old data?
+- Who is the data owner for each category?
+- When is data deleted and under what conditions?
+- The backup strategy in STORAGE.md marks several items as "Unknown" (e.g.,
+  Gitea repos backup target).
+- No single "data catalogue" document exists.
+
+**Blocks:** No — individual services have adequate backup. The lifecycle gap
+becomes a blocker only when data grows beyond the NAS capacity (89% today).
+
+**Next:** Create a data catalogue that maps data categories to owner, retention,
+backup method, and deletion policy. Resolve the "Unknown" entries in STORAGE.md.
+
