+## 8. Subsystem Boundaries and Contracts
+
+**Status:** `partially resolved`
+
+**Evidence:**
+- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` (lines 93–166) — Dispatch system with pattern→handler
+  registration, plugin auto-loading, handler signature convention.
+- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` (lines 168–230) — Worker system with GPU lock, Ollama
+  models, GitOps system with conflict resolution.
+- `docs/adr/006-approved-service-release-handoff.md` — Formal release contract:
+  CI emits SHA-bound request → operator approves → Lydia deploys → evidence
+  published.
+- `docs/service-release-contract.md` — Service lifecycle from PR CI through
+  operator approval to post-deployment smoke tests. Schema-validated JSON
+  request/result contracts.
+- `docs/decisions/playwright/evidence-provenance.md` — Extremely detailed
+  contract for manifest v1, trusted input envelope, runtime provenance, schema
+  evolution.
+- `docs/decisions/playwright/runner-bootstrap.md` — Complete Docker invocation
+  contract with every argument pinned.
+- `docs/matrix/proxy.md`, `docs/matrix/keycloak-oidc.md`, `docs/matrix/element.md` —
+  Per-component contracts specifying network, proxy, auth, and deployment
+  boundaries.
+
+**Gap:** Contracts are very strong for:
+- The Playwright test platform (pinned images, argument-for-argument contracts)
+- Service releases (formal handoff with schema validation)
+- Matrix components (per-service runbooks)
+
+Contracts are implicit or absent for:
+- The NAS interface: what exactly does the architecture expect from YeraNAS?
+  NFS is documented at the protocol level but no SLA or contract.
+- Inter-agent communication: Slarti ↔ Lydia communication is described but not
+  formally contracted (e.g., message schema, retry policy, timeout).
+- Plugin API: the handler signature is documented but no formal plugin API
+  version or compatibility contract.
+
+**Blocks:** No — existing contracts are sufficient for the current operational
+scale. The contract gap becomes a blocker only when third-party or external
+developers need to integrate.
+
+**Next:** Formalise the plugin API contract and add a versioning scheme.
+Document the NAS service-level expectation (minimum throughput, maximum
+latency, availability target).
